      "id": 10,
      "options": {
        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "**How the signals are derived**\n\n- **Crashes** are log lines matching backtrace, panic, core dump, segmentation fault, unhandled exception or fatal error. No Guile process introspection is involved.\n- **Restarts** are inferred from startup-looking log lines (`listening on`, `started`, `ready to serve`). The Shepherd does not publish start/stop counters, so a daemon that restarts silently, or logs nothing at startup, will not be counted. A gap in **Log lines read per daemon** is the complementary signal.\n- **Missing log streams** come from Alloy's per-file counters in Prometheus: if a file stops being tailed, its series disappears. The matching alert is gated on Alloy being up so an Alloy restart does not alert for every daemon at once.\n- **Quiet is not the same as broken**: a daemon with no traffic produces no lines. The alerting rules only fire on crash markers, repeated errors and lost files.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "title": "Reading this dashboard",
      "type": "text"
